# Parallel full test suite

When you run tests, run the full suite in parallel. The only allowed pytest command is:

```bash
uv run pytest
```

`pyproject.toml` addopts already set `-n auto` (pytest-xdist) and coverage. Do not override that.

Do not:

- Pass a file, directory, or node id (`tests/test_foo.py`, `tests/test_foo.py::test_bar`)
- Filter with `-k`, `-m`, `--lf`, `--ff`, `--sw`, or `-x`
- Disable workers (`-n0`, `-n 0`, `-n 1`, `-p no:xdist`)
- Clear addopts (`-o addopts=`, `--override-ini addopts=`)

A subset or a serial run is not a completed check. If a single test failed, still re-run `uv run pytest`.

E2E files under `tests/e2e/` are skipped unless the app is up. Do not replace the suite with an e2e file plus `-o addopts=`.
